      "writtenOn": "2024-05-30T21:05:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To be extra careful, you should probably make sure that `profileGroupId` isn\u0027t equal to `UserInfo.NO_PROFILE_GROUP_ID` first.\n\nActually, instead of checking `isFull` or `isProfile`, you could probably just check that `profileGroupId !\u003d NO_PROFILE_GROUP_ID` \u0026\u0026 profileGroupId !\u003d userId`, if you\u0027d prefer.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 484,
        "startChar": 70,
        "endLine": 484,
        "endChar": 84
      },
      "revId": "0c626e287b797ead24e67d0adc02642f0890254a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a24cbdd5_ec196a6d",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/locksettings/RebootEscrowManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 484,
      "author": {
        "id": 1165283
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-30T21:05:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Don\u0027t you need to do this in a *second* for loop, not the same for loop as above? I don\u0027t think there\u0027s a guarantee that the parent user comes before the profile, in which case the parent may not have been added to `fullUsersNoEscrowData` prior to the profile being considered.\n\nThat is, the first for loop only handles the `full` users, and then a second for loop would handle the `profile` users.\n\n[An alternative that just uses one for-loop would be to re-calculate `userHasEscrowData`, etc., on the profile\u0027s parent.]",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 484,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 484,
        "endChar": 14
      },
      "revId": "0c626e287b797ead24e67d0adc02642f0890254a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
